From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omarchy-dragon-sl7 <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] SL7: usb: typec: mux: ps883x: Optionally keep the PHY orientation fixed

SL7: usb: typec: mux: ps883x: Optionally keep the PHY orientation fixed

On the Surface Laptop 7, USB3 SuperSpeed fails to train whenever the
plug is reversed, on both USB-C ports: the link goes Polling to Inactive
in a warm-reset loop and never falls back to high speed. Normal
orientation works. Flipping only the retimer bit (REG0 0x21 with the
QMP combo PHY reversed) fails as well, and the XO change in 0070 is
cleared as the cause.

The Microsoft firmware on the PS8830 retimer already performs the
Type-C flip, so the QMP PHY has to stay in normal orientation whatever
the plug does.

Add the module parameter fixed_phy_orientation, on by default. While it
is set and the orientation is not TYPEC_ORIENTATION_NONE,
ps883x_sw_set() forwards TYPEC_ORIENTATION_NORMAL to the downstream
switch (the QMP combo PHY). The retimer's own orientation state and the
ORIENTATION_REVERSED bit in REG0 still follow the real plug.

Confirmed on the Surface Laptop 7: reverse SuperSpeed works on both
ports in both orientations, and DisplayPort alt mode and a dock work.
Disable with ps883x.fixed_phy_orientation=0 on the kernel command line.

Rationale: SL7 local, hardware evidence from 2026-10-06 replug captures
and on-device confirmation.

Origin: ours
Upstream-Status: Not submitted. SL7 specific (firmware-dependent).
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/mux/ps883x.c b/drivers/usb/typec/mux/ps883x.c
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/mux/ps883x.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/mux/ps883x.c
@@ -349,13 +349,26 @@ static int ps883x_set(struct ps883x_retimer *retimer, struct typec_retimer_state
 	return ps883x_configure(retimer, cfg0, cfg1, cfg2, reset);
 }
 
+/*
+ * SL7: the retimer firmware performs the Type-C flip, so USB3 SuperSpeed only
+ * trains on a reversed plug if the QMP PHY stays in normal orientation. On by
+ * default; ps883x.fixed_phy_orientation=0 restores plug-following.
+ */
+static bool fixed_phy_orientation = true;
+module_param(fixed_phy_orientation, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(fixed_phy_orientation, "Retimer performs the Type-C flip; keep the downstream QMP PHY in normal orientation (default: true; 0 makes the PHY follow the plug)");
+
 static int ps883x_sw_set(struct typec_switch_dev *sw,
 			 enum typec_orientation orientation)
 {
 	struct ps883x_retimer *retimer = typec_switch_get_drvdata(sw);
+	enum typec_orientation phy_orientation = orientation;
 	int ret = 0;
 
-	ret = typec_switch_set(retimer->typec_switch, orientation);
+	if (fixed_phy_orientation && orientation != TYPEC_ORIENTATION_NONE)
+		phy_orientation = TYPEC_ORIENTATION_NORMAL;
+
+	ret = typec_switch_set(retimer->typec_switch, phy_orientation);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
